Mix ingredients except methanol, NaHCO<sub>3</sub> and Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O, bring to a boil and cool down under a stream of N<sub>2</sub> gas.  Add methanol to the medium and distribute into culture vessels (e.g., 20 ml of the medium in 120 ml serum bottles) under a stream of H<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (4:1, v/v) gas mixture, seal with butyl rubber stoppers, and autoclave.  Separately autoclave 5% Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O solution under a N<sub>2</sub> atmosphere.  Filer-sterilize 8% NaHCO3 solution and store under a N<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (4:1, v/v) gas mixture.  Before inoculation, add the sterile NaHCO<sub>3</sub> and Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O solutions to the medium, and readjust pH to 7.0, if necessary. Pressurize the inoculated bottles to 200 kPa H<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (4:1, v/v).  <br>
